detector_raw:
{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this production plan — are we maximizing total profit (unit price minus raw material cost, with the operating costs treated as fixed full-capacity charges that do not depend on how much each machine is used), or is there a different objective such as maximizing revenue or minimizing cost?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting alternatives within one coherent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The operating costs are fixed charges incurred when a machine is used at all — is this a per-period charge (i.e., if any product is processed on that machine during the planning period, the full cost is incurred once), or is it a per-unit charge (i.e., the cost is incurred for each unit processed on that machine)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice between two mutually exclusive cost structures (per-period vs. per-unit), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are there any demand constraints or minimum production requirements for each product, or is the only constraint the machine capacity (effective machine hours)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the nature of the constraints (demand/minimums vs. machine capacity only)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For each product, must it be processed on exactly one machine for procedure A and exactly one machine for procedure B (i.e., all units of a given product go to a single machine per procedure), or can the units of a single product be split across multiple eligible machines for the same procedure?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether product units must be assigned to a single machine or can be split across multiple machines for each procedure."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since each product must go through both procedure A and procedure B, is there any constraint that the number of units completing procedure A must equal the number completing procedure B for each product (i.e., no work-in-progress or inventory of partially completed units), or can the quantities differ between the two procedures?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the flow balance between two procedures, presenting a binary choice (equal quantities vs. differing quantities) that constitutes one independent semantic query."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the production quantities for each product required to be whole numbers (integer units), or can they be fractional (continuous) values?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the variable type (integer vs. continuous) for production quantities."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "does \"used at all\" mean any positive amount of processing time on that machine triggers the full cost, or is there a minimum threshold of usage below which the cost is not incurred?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy definition regarding the trigger condition for the operating cost, presenting two mutually exclusive options for the same variable."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any limit on the total number of units that can be produced overall, or is the only upper bound on production the machine capacity (effective machine hours)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the upper bound on production, presenting two mutually exclusive options for the same constraint."
}
